LOGBOOK.md:399:- MECHANISM (leaf-2 item closed here): the derived refusal-arm inventory parses production AST — every `&frameFault` literal, every literal `integrity(...)` argument (with the `decodeStrictObject`-fault wrapper expanded over the derived frame detail set), every `parseMajor` rejection branch keyed by enclosing condition, and every literal first argument to the six refusal constructors — and checks both directions (every derived arm witnessed, every witness derived) plus a census floor. This leaf raised the floor 60 → 162 and added 102 witnesses, one per new arm.
LOGBOOK.md:451:- F1 (live spec violation): `CheckOperation("manifest"|"probe")` refused `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` even fully admitted; §4.D gives both `Capability dependencies: none` and neither row allows that code. Pinned by `TestCheckOperationAdmitsDependencyFreeOperations` (empty + full admitted sets, plus the still-refused gated operation).
LOGBOOK.md:578:- BOUND, stated rather than glossed: the harness mutates the working tree, so it lives under `.temp/` and is attached to the board item. `go test ./...` does not run it and no committed artifact derives its counts. `README.md` now says so where it publishes them, instead of letting a harness figure sit beside gated ones and read as though it were gated too.
LOGBOOK.md:705:- ROOT CAUSE: `Canonicalize`'s doc comment claimed it "rejects malformed UTF-8, invalid surrogate escapes, duplicate object names, and non-I-JSON input". Three of the four were true. The fourth was not: RFC 8785 Section 3.2.2.3 serializes numbers through the ECMAScript `Number.prototype.toString` algorithm on the binary64 value, so `canonical.go` rounded `9007199254740993` to `9007199254740992`, `18446744073709551615` to `18446744073709552000`, and `1.0` to `1`. No live defect — the identity path is gated by `validateAXNumbers`, called from `prepareObjectIdentity` — but `Canonicalize` is exported, so the first external caller would have inherited a guarantee it does not provide. Audit finding N5, the last of the thirteen second-audit findings.
LOGBOOK.md:903:- ANOMALY, pre-existing on trunk and not introduced here: `README.md:450` claimed 30 executable acceptance cases while `ownership.v0.5.0.json` on the same commit carried 35. The prose count is not gated — `tracecheck` pins `AcceptanceCases` and the two CLI strings, nothing reads the README sentence — so it drifted five behind across four Story landings. Base and both leaf trees agree README should equal `len(acceptance_cases)`; the merged tree restores that at 38. An ungated derived count is a comment, and it decayed like one.
LOGBOOK.md:952:- DECISION: three boundary values are unreachable and declared, not dropped — a zero `sequence` and a zero `epoch` are refused by the positive-integer gate first. Each names its subsuming refusal and a test that must exist. The one function whose comparisons run at package initialization over the pinned catalog is exempted by name, and the exemption asserts from the sources that every caller of it is a package-level initializer that panics.
LOGBOOK.md:1169:- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/localstore/projection_refusal_inventory_test.go` derived expected refusal sites from the production AST but matched only `*ast.Ident` calls named `projectionRefusal`. Six live clauses written as bare `fmt.Errorf("%w: ...", ErrUnsafeOwnership)` or as delegated `verifyOwnerFileInfo`/`verifyOwnerDirectory` guards were invisible to the gate whose job was to notice them, and shipped unpinned while 20+ funnelled sites were enforced.
LOGBOOK.md:1203:- FINDING (F1): The refusal-arm derivation walked FuncDecl bodies only, so a package-level `var f = func() *Error {…}` arm and an aliased constructor (`refuse := mismatchf`) each shipped reachable with a new detail while both inventory tests stayed green. Both shapes measured empty in the tree, so the 193/193 ratio held while the closure claim did not.
LOGBOOK.md:1204:- FIX (F1, preferred over a caveat): the derivation now scans every FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer (attributed to the variable name), and `rejectConstructorAliases` fatals on any constructor reference outside direct-call position. Replayed both reviewer probes copy-aside with shasum-verified restore: A1 fails the bijection (194 derived vs 193 rows), A2 fatals at the alias. Zero table change — both shapes are still empty in the tree.
LOGBOOK.md:1214:- FINDING (G2): `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` walked FuncDecl bodies only — the exact walk `deriveRefusalArms` was extended past in round 1, 200 lines above in the same file. Identical `errors.New` text was red in a FuncDecl and green in a package-level var (W5b), `fmt.Errorf` likewise (W9b), var func literal likewise (W16).
LOGBOOK.md:1215:- FIX (G2): the sibling walk gained the same GenDecl/ValueSpec loop (shared `isPlainErrorConstruction` helper, receiver-qualified method names). Twin-hunt over the story boundary (`internal/terminalbackend` AST walks): `deriveRefusalArms` already extended, `rejectConstructorAliases` inspects whole files, `productionCodeSymbols` walks package-level const GenDecls by construction, `testBodies`/`predicateCodes` are func-scoped by convention and fail closed, the platform funnel is function-scoped by design. No other twin. Bonus kill: an unused package-level plain-error var (W18 shape) is now red too — its initializer runs at package init, so the construction is real.
LOGBOOK.md:1236:- ANOMALY: the first gate version used `switch` and reddened `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` — the package census bans switches as membership-gate hiding spots. Rewritten with if/else, identical verdicts, green. A gate's own residue rules apply to the fix too.
LOGBOOK.md:1237:- ROOT CAUSE (B4): `tracecheck` verifies registry -> code only, so ~3,700 lines of `internal/provider` + `internal/provhost` landed with the gate green under gap prose asserting "no provider manifest is implemented anywhere". The census enumerates what registered itself.
