+
+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev9 — CR8 narrowing closures for typed write census and Store-owned Config binding
+- BASE: unchanged from rev8: candidate checkpoint `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d`, protected AX trunk `8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. The 15-file RPC backup manifest, parked RPC delta, and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain preserved; no RPC implementation path was absorbed.
+- FIX (F1): the production-source write-path census now resolves `go/types` function identities for bare identifiers and selectors, while rejecting writer-shaped indirect callees unless they are an exact censused definition in the current Go build context. The census rejects dot-imported function values, promoted embedded backend methods, package-level slice writer functions, function-typed struct fields and parameters, and dot-imported composite-literal function values. `isHoldEntryCall` uses exact package/receiver/method identity, so a same-named impostor method is not an entry gate.
+- FIX (F2): `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig` is Store-owned. A generic or foreign Store cannot bind an arbitrary existing Config path; a configured Store can bind only its canonical paired path. Refusal occurs before staging/bytes mutation. The narrowing mutant drops the unconfigured-store refusal while retaining the other path checks and is killed by `TestWithExclusiveHoldForConfigRefusesUnconfiguredStorePath`.
